WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.843 --> 00:00:02.260
RETO MEIER: It's
officially Week 4

00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:04.300
of Google Cloud Next
OnAir, which means

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:06.530
we're focusing on security.

00:00:06.530 --> 00:00:08.650
I'm Reto Meier, and welcome
to This Week in Cloud,

00:00:08.650 --> 00:00:12.430
where we're taking a sneak
peek at this week's content.

00:00:12.430 --> 00:00:15.160
Week 4 is all about
security, meaning

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:17.320
we want to help you
achieve your security

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:20.200
goals while prioritizing
operational simplicity

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.010
and keeping costs down.

00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:24.760
So we've got sessions on
everything from data protection

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:28.340
to compliance policies to
managing sensitive data.

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:31.510
You can also hear directly from
other Google Cloud customers

00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:34.540
sharing their own
security experiences.

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:36.670
One of the best parts of
attending a conference

00:00:36.670 --> 00:00:38.860
is learning the
clever and sneaky tips

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:42.440
from some of the people who
actually created the products.

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:45.700
That's why this advanced IM
session is so compelling,

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:49.220
because authentication and
policy management are constant.

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:51.640
So a deep dive into
advanced controls

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:56.170
sounds like a great way to avoid
future policy change conflicts.

00:00:56.170 --> 00:01:00.010
My pick for the week is Getting
Started with BeyondCorp,

00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:03.010
because I really like it when we
can share the tools that Google

00:01:03.010 --> 00:01:04.900
is actually running on.

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:07.930
That's the Google Cloud
origin story after all.

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:10.870
And this session introduces
the BeyondCorp security model

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:12.940
and how shifting your
security protections

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:15.190
from a physical
perimeter-- like, say,

00:01:15.190 --> 00:01:18.730
your office building-- to
individual accounts and devices

00:01:18.730 --> 00:01:22.300
allows your employees to work
remotely without a VPN, which

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:26.840
may be particularly useful to
you in this nonsense of a year.

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:29.120
Finally, if you're looking
to hone your skills,

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:30.580
be sure to check
out to Cloud Study

00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:32.440
Jam, where you can
join other attendees

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:34.630
for guided hands-on labs.

00:01:34.630 --> 00:01:36.130
There are several
options this week,

00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:39.070
including HTTP Load
Balancer with Cloud Armor

00:01:39.070 --> 00:01:42.445
and User Authentication,
Identity-Aware Proxy.

00:01:42.445 --> 00:01:46.450
Be sure to register for a study
jam to learn from an expert.

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:48.850
To add these sessions to
your digital playlist,

00:01:48.850 --> 00:01:50.210
check out the link.

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:51.520
Any thoughts or ideas?

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:53.980
Leave us a comment or
tweet us using the hashtag

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:55.600
#GoogleCloudNext.

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:58.290
We'll see you in the cloud.

